---
import { SOCIAL_MEDIA } from "@/constants/social-media";
import Layout from "@/layouts/base/layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl pb-10 md:pb-0 xl:pb-10">
    <div>
      <h3 class="mb-4">About me</h3>
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Aleksa Ćuković - a software engineer from Montenegro, living in
        Amsterdam. I enjoy learning, solving problems and building things. I
        especially like building stuff that I can use myself, which is why I
        prefer to work on infrastructure and developer tooling. When I'm not
        working I'm hacking on my side projects, hanging out with friends and
        family, watching TV shows, lifting weights, playing basketball or
        traveling. To see what I've been up to lately, check out my
        <a href="now/">now page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="mt-8 mb-4">About my work</h3>
      <p>
        I work as a site reliability engineer at FareHarbor - one of the
        lesser-known companies in the Booking Holdings portfolio. If you've ever
        booked a tour or activity online, there's a high chance our platform was
        what made that possible. Before that, I worked at smaller companies in
        Montenegro and did a lot of freelance work, mostly for small companies
        and startups.
        <br />
        <br />
        I like open source software and have made many small contributions to various
        projects and open sourced some of my own work. Most of it is available on
        my <a href={SOCIAL_MEDIA.github.link}>GitHub account</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="mt-8 mb-4">About this website</h3>
      <p>
        My goals with this website have changed a bit over time, though they
        haven't really been clear at any point. I've seen a bunch of great
        personal websites and read many great posts on them, so I guess I wanted
        something like that for myself. Unfortunately I haven't been able to
        dedicate the time and effort to make this into a reality yet, so for now
        this website mostly serves as an introduciton to myself that I can
        reference across different point of my online presence.
        <br />
        <br />
        The main technical constraints I optimized for while building this website
        were that it should be easy to develop and maintain, fast, and as cheap as
        possible to host. I'm thankful for Astro and Cloudflare Pages for making it
        easy to achieve this goal. Both the code and content for this website live
        in a
        <a href="https://github.com/AleksaC/aleksac.me">public GitHub repo</a>,
        so you can open issues if you come across any.
        <br />
        <br />
        The first iteration of this website predates the LLM era, and the majority
        of the development work on it was done before LLMs were good at writing code,
        so it's still entirely hand-crafted. I intend to keep it that way, mostly
        because I don't use AI for writing (other than proofreading) and I'm not planning
        to do any development other than small tweaks that are probably easier to
        do by hand.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="mt-8 mb-4">Contact</h3>
      <p>
        If you'd like to reach out, feel free to send me an email at
        <a href="mailto:hello@aleksac.me">hello@aleksac.me</a>. Since I've
        mostly had positive experiences with people reaching out, my DMs are
        open, and you can contact me on
        <a href={SOCIAL_MEDIA.twitter.link}>Twitter</a> and
        <a href={SOCIAL_MEDIA.instagram.link}>Instagram</a>. You can also
        connect with me on <a href={SOCIAL_MEDIA.linkedin.link}>LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
